---
import type { Product } from '../../../data/products';
import CapabilityGrid from '../CapabilityGrid.astro';
import UseCases from '../UseCases.astro';
import Limits from '../Limits.astro';
import PlatformArchitecture from '../diagrams/PlatformArchitecture.astro';
import ChatToAction from '../diagrams/ChatToAction.astro';

interface Props {
  product: Product;
}

const { product } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="mt-20 grid gap-10 border-t border-hairline pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.8fr)_minmax(0,1.2fr)]">
  <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.18em] text-cobalt">What Platform is</p>
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    {product.overview.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
    <p>
      The runtime is built around agents, specialist agent teams, tools, knowledge, workflows, controlled autonomy, human escalation, integration, and the production operations that make those things operable. A chatbot framework with a different label is not enough.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-20">
  <div class="mb-8 max-w-2xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Core architecture</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-[1.35rem] font-medium tracking-tight">
      From a request to a governed action.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      A user, an event or an upstream system enters an agent router. Work is handed to a specialist team, which uses tools, workflows, retrieval and memory. Those agents sit on top of existing enterprise systems and knowledge sources. Escalation, observability and governance remain in the path.
    </p>
  </div>
  <PlatformArchitecture />
</section>

<div class="mt-20">
  <CapabilityGrid items={product.capabilities} />
</div>

<div class="mt-24">
  <UseCases
    items={product.useCases}
    title="Work the runtime is designed to carry"
  />
</div>

<section class="mt-24">
  <div class="mb-8 max-w-2xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">From interface to action</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-[1.35rem] font-medium tracking-tight">
      A chatbot is an interface. Platform is the operating system behind it.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      A basic chatbot replies. A retrieval assistant grounds that reply in documents. An operational agent can use tools, run workflows and coordinate a team. Many teams buy the first of these and later find they needed the last. The progression is what Platform is for.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ChatToAction />
  <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-8 border-t border-hairline pt-10 md:grid-cols-3">
    <li>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-cobalt">Chat</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        A conversational interface. Useful, and usually not enough on its own.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-cobalt">Retrieval assistant</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Answers drawn from approved knowledge, with citations and refusal when the corpus does not support the claim.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-cobalt">Operational agent</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Tools, workflows and specialist teams that can complete work — and escalate when they should not.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="mt-24 max-w-2xl">
  <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.18em] text-muted">Deployment model</p>
  <h2 class="mt-3 text-[1.35rem] font-medium tracking-tight">
    Adapted to the organisation you already have.
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Platform is deployed around the systems, APIs, knowledge bases, security requirements, workflows, identity models and cloud environments you already run. The product is the runtime and the method. The shape of a given deployment is yours.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Hosting, identity and compliance follow the environment you already run. We do not claim a single hosting or certification posture for every deployment.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Specialist products apply the same operating system to a particular domain.
    {' '}
    <a href="/products/callcenter" class="text-ink hover:text-cobalt">Callcenter</a>
    {' '}
    is the customer-service product: voice, messaging, email and human handoff on the same agentic principles.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="mt-20">
  <Limits items={product.limits} title="Controlled autonomy, with a person in the path where it is needed." />
</div>
